-- Std.Yield: just the effect that `Std.Stream` is built on.
--
-- It lives in its own module for one reason: a collection's `toStream` has to
-- perform `yield`, and `Std.Stream`'s consumers (`toVec`, `ofVec`, …) have to
-- know about the collections. Both cannot be the earlier module, so the effect
-- goes first on its own and everything else can depend on it.
--
-- Reach it through `Std.Stream`, which re-exports `yield` -- there is no reason
-- to name this module directly.

@pub effect Yield a {
  yield : a -> Unit,
}
